&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Gut, Your Health: A Colon Cancer Awareness Talk&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Featuring Sharmitha Yerneni, MD and&amp;nbsp;Sheila D. Rustgi, MD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;March is Colon Cancer Awareness Month &amp;mdash; a timely opportunity to learn how simple steps can lead to life-saving prevention. This community-focused talk is designed for CUIMC and NYP employees who want clear, accessible information about colon health and cancer screening.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join &lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sheila D. Rustgi&lt;/strong&gt;, a leading expert in gastroenterology, and &lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sharmitha Yerneni&lt;/strong&gt;, resident physician, for a straightforward conversation on what colon cancer is, how to reduce your risk, when to get screened, and how to talk about it with your loved ones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you&amp;rsquo;re new to the topic or looking to refresh your knowledge, this session offers practical tools and expert insight &amp;mdash; all in a welcoming environment built to support your health and your voice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Because the more we know, the more lives we can save &amp;mdash; starting with our own.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hosted by Women in Medicine at Columbia in collaboration&amp;nbsp;with the &lt;a href="https://www.acp.cuimc.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;CUIMC Office of Academic and Community Partnerships&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Human Rights in an Aging World: Technology, Inclusion, and Accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Join the Columbia Law School Human Rights Institute for a timely conversation with&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Dr. Claudia Mahler&lt;/strong&gt;, UN Independent Expert on the enjoyment of all human rights by older persons. The discussion will explore how digitalization, artificial intelligence, data privacy, and emerging technologies are redefining equality, autonomy, and dignity in later life &amp;mdash; and what role lawyers can play in shaping rights-based responses.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Dr. Mahler will also share insights from her UN mandate and discuss pathways for student engagement in cutting-edge research and advocacy at the intersection of human rights, technology, and aging.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Speaker&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dr. Claudia Mahler, UN Independent Expert on the enjoyment of all human rights by older persons&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When&lt;/strong&gt;: Tuesday,&amp;nbsp;March 10, 2026; 12:10 am-1:10 pm&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Where&lt;/strong&gt;: Columbia Law School, JG 107&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
