&lt;p&gt;In recognition of Women&amp;rsquo;s History Month, University Life invites you to join us for an excursion to the &lt;a href="https://www.tenement.org/neighborhood-walking-tours/?utm_source=SEM&amp;amp;utm_medium=google&amp;amp;utm_campaign=tenement_museum_2024&amp;amp;gad_source=1&amp;amp;gad_campaignid=20928008133&amp;amp;gbraid=0AAAAAqunyVpbH6-M8Uc4MH2Iv6jmJZXZz&amp;amp;gclid=Cj0KCQiAhOfLBhCCARIsAJPiopP1muOKtxSfSa3gYbJzBQ_TNYi-9XAZaiyTTVnteHnt93OiYxTbl8YaAvG9EALw_wcB"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tenement Museum&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; on the Lower East Side, honoring the women who labored tirelessly to build better lives for themselves and their communities in early 20th-century New York City.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the &lt;strong&gt;Legacy of New York&lt;/strong&gt; series, this guided tour brings to life the experiences of women who navigated strict gender roles and economic hardship. We&amp;rsquo;ll visit the &lt;a href="https://www.tenement.org/lesson_plans/the-levine-family-story/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Levine Family&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s 325-square-foot apartment, where Polish-Jewish immigrants &lt;strong&gt;Jennie Levine &lt;/strong&gt;and her family built a new life full of dreams for a brighter future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through this experience, we&amp;rsquo;ll discover how women collectively advocated for their families and communities at a time where they faced consistent exclusion. From the &lt;strong&gt;Kosher Meat Boycott of 1902&lt;/strong&gt; to the &lt;strong&gt;Uprising of the 20,000 in 1909&lt;/strong&gt;, we&amp;rsquo;ll gain a deeper understanding of how these women shaped and inspired generational change.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Legacy of New York&lt;/strong&gt; series invites students to explore the social movements, histories, and communities that have shaped New York City. Through museum visits, walking tours, and site-based learning experiences, this series seeks to highlight and celebrate the diversity of communities, cultures, and events.&lt;/p&gt;
